From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: keep Matisse firmware console until KMS takeover

Retain the verified RGB888 firmware framebuffer for the early console in
the native profile. Its clock and power-domain references keep the inherited
display alive before late native driver activation. MSM KMS already calls
aperture_remove_all_conflicting_devices() before initializing its display
engine, so simplefb releases its mapping and references at native takeover.

This does not enable simpledrm or route Plasma through firmware scanout.
Native KWin continues to select the MDP5 device explicitly. Panel power and
suspend validation remain incomplete; a seamless handoff is not claimed.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
@@ -3,7 +3,8 @@
 #include "qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts"
 
 &framebuffer0 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	/* Boot console only; msm_drm_kms_init removes the firmware aperture. */
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &mdp_smmu {
